module inventory/build attestations/test results, submitted through security review board to lab; NOT \"certification granted\". Risks: lab turnaround 6-9 months, review-board cadence — externally controlled.\n- E004: Documentation of FIPS support posture and cluster prerequisites (HLR-4). implementation_type: docs-authoring. Component: Documentation. Team: ??? P0 (docs exception, strategy Critical). Dependencies: E001, E002, E003 (Rule 11: blocked by ALL Implementation epics). AC: technically reviewed against implementation (Rule 24).\n\nWait — Rule 11 says docs-authoring blocked by ALL Implementation epics in strategy. E001-E003 are all Implementations. So E004 depends on all three. OK.\n\nNow HLR-3 bundling: the traceability matrix must flag \"(bundled)\" with inline rationale. HLR-3 rows: E001 (KServe builds) and E002 (Platform Operator builds) — each with bundled rationale: the gating check guards the same image builds the P0 remediation converts; shared surface (same builds/CI), splitting would duplicate.\n\nHmm wait, actually, is HLR-3 really \"bundled\"? HLR-3 is P1, the remediation is P0. The enforcement is per-surface divided into the consuming epics. So yes — bundled per the shared-surface enforcement rule.\n\nNow, the module inventory for the evidence package — should there be an Investigation \"audit which images link non-validated crypto\"? The strategy asserts it as known: \"several images link non-validated crypto libraries\". The precise list is an implementation detail discovered during the work. Doesn't change epic existence/shape (remediation epic covers whichever images are affected). Fold into E001/E002 scope (\"audit images for non-validated crypto usage; remediate findings\"). Good.\n\nTeams: Let me search the repo for team names used elsewhere (docs/, skills). Let me check the validator too, plus frontmatter.py schema for epic-task to know allowed fields.\n\nFor Platform Operator team — hmm. Since no Impacted Teams table exists and no archit