{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-f312ae31-7c36-46f5-8186-401f3d0c63be","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9588987d1f6deab8","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9013-1ngiuyxm/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9013-decomposition.md","content":"# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9013: FIPS 140-3 compliance for the model serving stack\n\nThe strategy is decomposed into four Implementation epics. Two parallel remediation\nepics (one per affected component) make the serving-stack images FIPS-compliant and\ncarry the per-surface CI regression gates; a compliance evidence epic assembles and\nsubmits the certification package once the images are compliant; a documentation\nepic closes the strategy. No Investigation epics are generated: the strategy\nexplicitly declares no open questions on scope, and the image/crypto audit does not\nchange which epics exist or what they do (remediation covers whatever the audit\nfinds — fix-and-retry, per the implementation-detail vs. genuine-unknown rule).\n\n## Epic List\n\n| ID | Title | Type | Component | Team | Priority |\n|----|-------|------|-----------|------|----------|\n| RHAISTRAT-9013-E001 | FIPS 140-3 crypto module remediation for KServe serving-stack images | Implementation | KServe | RHOAI Serving | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9013-E002 | FIPS 140-3 crypto module remediation for Platform Operator images | Implementation | Platform Operator | RHOAI Serving | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9013-E003 | FIPS 140-3 compliance evidence package and certification submission | Implementation | KServe | RHOAI Serving | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9013-E004 | Document the FIPS support posture and cluster prerequisites for the model serving stack | Implementation (docs-authoring) | Documentation | RHOAI Serving | P0 |\n\n## Dependency DAG\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    E001[\"E001 KServe image remediation (P0)\"] --> E003[\"E003 Evidence package + submission (P0)\"]\n    E002[\"E002 Platform Operator image remediation (P0)\"] --> E003\n    E001 --> E004[\"E004 FIPS documentation (docs-authoring)\"]\n    E002 --> E004\n    E003 --> E004\n```\n\nE001 and E002 are roots and run in parallel. The longest path\n(E001 → E003 → E004, equivalently E002 → E003 → E004) contains 4 epics.\n\n## DAG Justification\n\n| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n|------|------|-----------|\n| E001 ∥ E002 (no edge) | Rule 14 | Different components in different repos, no shared artifacts — the remediations are independent and must run in parallel. |\n| E001 → E003 | Rule 13 | The evidence package is assembled from the remediation deliverables (module inventory, build attestations, FIPS verification test results) and must reflect the final compliant images, so it is serial after the KServe remediation. |\n| E002 → E003 | Rule 13 | Same as above for the Platform Operator remediation — the package cannot truthfully describe a compliant serving stack until both components are remediated. |\n| E001 → E004 | Rule 11 | docs-authoring epic is blocked by every Implementation epic in the strategy; documentation describes what was built. |\n| E002 → E004 | Rule 11 | Same. |\n| E003 → E004 | Rule 11 | Same. |\n\nNotes on edges that deliberately do NOT exist:\n\n- No `konflux-onboarding` epic is generated, so Rules 7/8/10/25 do not apply.\n  KServe is already Konflux-onboarded (per\n  `.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.0/kserve.md`); the strategy\n  does not ask to onboard any new repo or pipeline.\n- Build attestations reach the evidence package as content via an acceptance\n  criterion on E003 (\"the package includes the build attestations produced by the\n  components' build pipelines\"), not via a DAG edge — the Rule 13\n  configuration/content carve-out.\n- The externally-controlled certification process (lab turnaround, review-board\n  cadence) is recorded as risks on E003, never as DAG edges or acceptance\n  criteria.\n\n##