{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-a65ef4fa-dc23-4eba-bf1f-78a54b2b1f6c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b428191bb209d8a8","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9013-1ngiuyxm/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9013-E003.md","content":"# FIPS 140-3 compliance evidence package and certification submission\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic assembles the FIPS 140-3 compliance evidence package for the model\nserving stack — module inventory, build attestations, and test results — and\ndrives it through the mandatory security review board milestones to submission\nat the external accredited certification laboratory. It is the strategy's\ncompliance-delivery epic: its engineering deliverable ends at a complete,\nreviewed, submitted, and triaged evidence package.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Assemble the module inventory covering every serving-stack image (KServe and\n  Platform Operator), consolidated from the component-level audits.\n- Collect the build attestations produced by the serving-stack components'\n  build pipelines for the remediated images.\n- Collect the FIPS verification test results demonstrating correct operation\n  of the remediated images on FIPS-enabled OpenShift clusters.\n- Structure and package the evidence according to the certification\n  requirements communicated by the security review board and the certification\n  lab.\n- Deliver the evidence required at each defined security review board\n  milestone and present it for sign-off.\n- Submit the final package to the external accredited certification lab and\n  track the submission through triage.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. The evidence package contains a complete module inventory covering every\n   serving-stack image (KServe and Platform Operator).\n2. The evidence package includes the build attestations produced by the\n   serving-stack components' build pipelines for the remediated images.\n3. The evidence package includes the test results demonstrating correct\n   operation of the remediated images on FIPS-enabled clusters.\n4. The evidence required at each defined security review board milestone is\n   delivered and presented (pass/fail per milestone).\n5. The final evidence package is submitted to the external certification lab\n   and the submission is acknowledged/triaged by the lab.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-2 (P0)** — the compliance evidence package (module inventory, build\n  attestations, test results) is assembled and submitted through the security\n  review board to the external certification lab.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Certification lab turnaround is historically six to nine months, and the\n  security review board meets on a fixed cadence; both are externally\n  controlled and cannot be compressed by engineering effort. They dominate the\n  program schedule and are recorded here as schedule risks — they are\n  deliberately not acceptance criteria. The certification grant itself is\n  outside this epic's engineering control; this epic's deliverable is the\n  submitted and triaged evidence package.\n- The package must reflect the final remediated images, so this epic runs\n  after the serving-stack image remediation is complete; late image changes\n  invalidate affected evidence and require re-collection.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":50574,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b969525f5991b86","agent_id":"a6cc13b92c28b7636","session_id":"f3804fb2-6446-43d6-8c27-86f0daf65430","uuid":"25054751-63d6-4af6-a82e-f84f2249cb14","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:11:01.512Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9013 into epics"}
