{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-a65ef4fa-dc23-4eba-bf1f-78a54b2b1f6c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-889e33afbb84103a","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9013-1ngiuyxm/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9013-E004.md","content":"# Document the FIPS support posture and cluster prerequisites for the model serving stack\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic authors the user-facing documentation for the FIPS 140-3 support of\nthe model serving stack: what the support posture is, and what cluster\nprerequisites apply for running the serving stack on FIPS-enabled OpenShift\nclusters. It runs last so the documentation describes what was actually built\nand verified.\n\n## Scope\n\nContent outline (to be authored inside the product documentation):\n\n- FIPS support posture of the model serving stack: which components and images\n  are FIPS-compliant, and what \"validated crypto modules\" means for the\n  request path.\n- Cluster prerequisites: FIPS-enabled OpenShift clusters, and any serving\n  mode considerations that affect the FIPS posture (serverless vs. raw\n  deployment dependencies).\n- Limitations and out-of-scope statements consistent with the strategy (no\n  coverage of workbenches, pipelines, training, or Common Common Criteria —\n  those are separate strategies).\n- Guidance on verifying FIPS operation (e.g., where the verification results\n  and posture claims come from).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. Published documentation states the FIPS support posture of the model\n   serving stack, consistent with the delivered implementation.\n2. Published documentation states the cluster prerequisites for running the\n   serving stack on FIPS-enabled OpenShift clusters.\n3. The documentation is technically reviewed against the delivered\n   implementation (review sign-off recorded).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-4 (P2)** — documentation states the FIPS support posture and cluster\n  prerequisites. Note: the epic's priority is derived from the strategy's\n  overall priority (Critical → P0) via the docs-authoring priority exception,\n  not from the HLR's P2 label.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- The documentation must not state a posture ahead of the certification\n  outcome: the posture documented is the engineering posture (validated crypto\n  modules in the request path, FIPS-enabled cluster operation), with the\n  certification status described as pending until the lab grants it.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":50574,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b969525f5991b86","agent_id":"a6cc13b92c28b7636","session_id":"f3804fb2-6446-43d6-8c27-86f0daf65430","uuid":"f151ecd3-5f2d-462c-91b4-6aa3e5773645","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:11:08.476Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9013 into epics"}
