{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-816655c9701fdc49","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9013-E002\n3\ttitle: FIPS 140-3 crypto module remediation for Platform Operator images\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9013\n5\tcomponent: Platform Operator\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 0\n19\t  architecture_claims: 0\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 3\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# FIPS 140-3 crypto module remediation for Platform Operator images\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers FIPS 140-3 compliance for the Platform Operator portion of\n34\tthe model serving stack. Every container image shipped by the Platform\n35\tOperator component is audited for non-validated cryptographic library usage,\n36\tremediated to use validated crypto modules, and verified to run correctly on\n37\tFIPS-enabled OpenShift clusters. The epic also carries the operator-side CI\n38\tregression gate so non-validated crypto usage cannot be reintroduced by future\n39\tbuilds.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Audit all container images shipped by the Platform Operator component and\n44\t  document every linkage to non-validated cryptographic libraries, with\n45\t  particular attention to the request path and the components of the serving\n46\t  data plane the operator deploys.\n47\t- Remediate each identified image so that no non-validated crypto is used in\n48\t  the request path, replacing it with validated cryptographic modules.\n49\t- Rebuild the remediated images through the component's existing build\n50\t  pipeline so that build attestations are produced for the compliant images.\n51\t- Verify that the remediated operator deploys and manages the serving stack\n52\t  correctly on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster, and collect the verification\n53\t  results.\n54\t- Add a gating CI check that fails any Platform Operator build that\n55\t  reintroduces non-validated crypto usage, wired into CI for those builds.\n56\t- Confirm no functional regression on non-FIPS clusters.\n57\t- Hand off the Platform Operator module inventory, build attestations, and\n58\t  verification results for inclusion in the compliance evidence package.\n59\t\n60\t## Acceptance Criteria\n61\t\n62\t1. A documented audit covers every Platform Operator image and identifies all\n63\t   non-validated crypto library linkages (pass/fail: the inventory exists and\n64\t   covers every image in scope).\n65\t2. Every image identified by the audit is remediated so that no non-validated\n66\t   crypto is used in the request path (pass/fail per image).\n67\t3. The remediated images build successfully in the component's existing build\n68\t   pipeline and produce build attestations.\n69\t4. Verification results demonstrate that the operator deploys and manages the\n70\t   model serving stack correctly on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster with the\n71\t   remediated images.\n72\t5. A gating CI check fails any Platform Operator build that reintroduces\n73\t   non-validated crypto usage, and the check is wired into CI for those\n74\t   builds (pass/fail: a deliberately non-compliant build fails the gate).\n75\t6. The remediated images show no functional regression on non-FIPS clusters.\n76\t\n77\t## HLR Traceability\n78\t\n79\t- **HLR-1 (P0)** — Platform Operator share: all Platform Operator images run\n80\t  correctly on FIPS-enabled clusters using validated crypto modules, with no\n81\t  non-validated crypto in the request path.\n82\t- **HLR-3 (P1, bundled)** — Platform Operator share of the FIPS regression CI\n83\t  enforcement: the gating check for operator builds is carried in this epic\n84\t  because it guards the same image builds this epic remediates (shared\n85\t  surface; not separately schedulable from the remediation it guards).\n86\t\n87\t## Risks / Notes\n88\t\n89\t- Verification on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster requires access to such a\n90\t  cluster; the acceptance criteria sit on the verification deliverables, and\n91\t  cluster access is an environment prerequisite to be secured during\n92\t  execution.\n93\t- The exact set of affected images and libraries is unknown until the audit\n94\t  runs; the remediation covers whatever the audit finds (fix-and-retry), which\n95\t  is why no separate investigation epic is needed.\n96\t- No architecture-context file exists for Platform Operator in the provided\n97\t  context; the component is treated as existing and shipping images today, per\n98\t  the strategy's premise. The owning team should be confirmed at plan time.\n99\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2ed01ab462c4bc2","agent_id":"a71369903f8174256","session_id":"f3804fb2-6446-43d6-8c27-86f0daf65430","uuid":"4fff6b81-4b36-483e-bef1-64b826de33f9","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:13:14.745Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-816655c9701fdc49","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
