{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92849faa54fbb828","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9013-E001\n3\ttitle: FIPS 140-3 crypto module remediation for KServe serving-stack images\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9013\n5\tcomponent: KServe\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 5\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# FIPS 140-3 crypto module remediation for KServe serving-stack images\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers FIPS 140-3 compliance for the KServe portion of the model\n34\tserving stack. Every container image shipped by the KServe component is audited\n35\tfor non-validated cryptographic library usage, remediated to use validated\n36\tcrypto modules, and verified to run correctly on FIPS-enabled OpenShift\n37\tclusters. The epic also carries the KServe-side CI regression gate so\n38\tnon-validated crypto usage cannot be reintroduced by future builds.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Audit all container images shipped by the KServe component (including the\n43\t  serving data plane images it deploys that belong to this component) and\n44\t  document every linkage to non-validated cryptographic libraries, with\n45\t  particular attention to the request path.\n46\t- Remediate each identified image so that no non-validated crypto is used in\n47\t  the request path, replacing it with validated cryptographic modules.\n48\t- Rebuild the remediated images through the component's existing build\n49\t  pipeline so that build attestations are produced for the compliant images.\n50\t- Verify that the remediated images serve inference requests correctly on a\n51\t  FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster, and collect the verification results.\n52\t- Add a gating CI check that fails any KServe serving-stack build that\n53\t  reintroduces non-validated crypto usage, wired into CI for those builds.\n54\t- Confirm no functional regression on non-FIPS clusters.\n55\t- Hand off the KServe module inventory, build attestations, and verification\n56\t  results for inclusion in the compliance evidence package.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t1. A documented audit covers every KServe serving-stack image and identifies\n61\t   all non-validated crypto library linkages (pass/fail: the inventory exists\n62\t   and covers every image in scope).\n63\t2. Every image identified by the audit is remediated so that no non-validated\n64\t   crypto is used in the request path (pass/fail per image).\n65\t3. The remediated images build successfully in the component's existing build\n66\t   pipeline and produce build attestations.\n67\t4. Verification results demonstrate that inference serving works correctly on\n68\t   a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster with the remediated images.\n69\t5. A gating CI check fails any KServe serving-stack build that reintroduces\n70\t   non-validated crypto usage, and the check is wired into CI for those\n71\t   builds (pass/fail: a deliberately non-compliant build fails the gate).\n72\t6. The remediated images show no functional regression on non-FIPS clusters.\n73\t\n74\t## HLR Traceability\n75\t\n76\t- **HLR-1 (P0)** — KServe share: all KServe serving-stack images run correctly\n77\t  on FIPS-enabled clusters using validated crypto modules, with no\n78\t  non-validated crypto in the request path.\n79\t- **HLR-3 (P1, bundled)** — KServe share of the FIPS regression CI enforcement:\n80\t  the gating check for KServe builds is carried in this epic because it guards\n81\t  the same image builds this epic remediates (shared surface; not separately\n82\t  schedulable from the remediation it guards).\n83\t\n84\t## Risks / Notes\n85\t\n86\t- Verification on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster requires access to such a\n87\t  cluster; the acceptance criteria sit on the verification deliverables, and\n88\t  cluster access is an environment prerequisite to be secured during\n89\t  execution.\n90\t- The exact set of affected images and libraries is unknown until the audit\n91\t  runs; the remediation covers whatever the audit finds (fix-and-retry), which\n92\t  is why no separate investigation epic is needed.\n93\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9463369e1a6e9580","agent_id":"ad1b8ad0f4d959631","session_id":"f3804fb2-6446-43d6-8c27-86f0daf65430","uuid":"6ac0543c-99d6-4e4d-b332-9535c2ca2428","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:18:35.297Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-92849faa54fbb828","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
