{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b43d006ee8ccb3e4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9013-E003\n3\ttitle: FIPS 140-3 compliance evidence package and certification submission\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9013\n5\tcomponent: KServe\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9013-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9013-E002\n12\tai_signals:\n13\t  change_specificity: 0\n14\t  pattern_precedent: -1\n15\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n16\t  existing_foundation: -1\n17\t  open_questions: 1\n18\t  external_dependency: -1\n19\t  human_process_gates: -1\n20\t  repo_access: 1\n21\t  architecture_claims: 1\n22\timplementation_type: null\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: Low\n25\tai_implementability_score: -1\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# FIPS 140-3 compliance evidence package and certification submission\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tThis epic assembles the FIPS 140-3 compliance evidence package for the model\n36\tserving stack — module inventory, build attestations, and test results — and\n37\tdrives it through the mandatory security review board milestones to submission\n38\tat the external accredited certification laboratory. It is the strategy's\n39\tcompliance-delivery epic: its engineering deliverable ends at a complete,\n40\treviewed, and submitted evidence package.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Assemble the module inventory covering every serving-stack image (KServe and\n45\t  Platform Operator), consolidated from the component-level audits.\n46\t- Collect the build attestations produced by the serving-stack components'\n47\t  build pipelines for the remediated images.\n48\t- Collect the FIPS verification test results demonstrating correct operation\n49\t  of the remediated images on FIPS-enabled OpenShift clusters.\n50\t- Structure and package the evidence according to the certification\n51\t  requirements communicated by the security review board and the certification\n52\t  lab.\n53\t- Deliver the evidence required at each defined security review board\n54\t  milestone and present it for sign-off.\n55\t- Submit the final package to the external accredited certification lab and\n56\t  track the submission status.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t1. The evidence package contains a complete module inventory covering every\n61\t   serving-stack image (KServe and Platform Operator).\n62\t2. The evidence package includes the build attestations produced by the\n63\t   serving-stack components' build pipelines for the remediated images.\n64\t3. The evidence package includes the test results demonstrating correct\n65\t   operation of the remediated images on FIPS-enabled clusters.\n66\t4. The evidence required at each defined security review board milestone is\n67\t   delivered and presented (pass/fail per milestone).\n68\t5. The final evidence package is submitted to the external certification lab\n69\t   (pass/fail: the submission is complete).\n70\t\n71\t## HLR Traceability\n72\t\n73\t- **HLR-2 (P0)** — the compliance evidence package (module inventory, build\n74\t  attestations, test results) is assembled and submitted through the security\n75\t  review board to the external certification lab.\n76\t\n77\t## Risks / Notes\n78\t\n79\t- Certification lab turnaround is historically six to nine months, and the\n80\t  security review board meets on a fixed cadence; both are externally\n81\t  controlled and cannot be compressed by engineering effort. They dominate the\n82\t  program schedule and are recorded here as schedule risks — they are\n83\t  deliberately not acceptance criteria. Lab acknowledgement and triage of the\n84\t  submission are likewise controlled by the external lab rather than by this\n85\t  epic's deliverable, so the acceptance criteria end at submission and\n86\t  acknowledgement/triage is tracked here as a follow-up risk. The\n87\t  certification grant itself is outside this epic's engineering control;\n88\t  this epic's deliverable is the submitted evidence package.\n89\t- The package must reflect the final remediated images, so this epic runs\n90\t  after the serving-stack image remediation is complete; late image changes\n91\t  invalidate affected evidence and require re-collection.\n92\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9463369e1a6e9580","agent_id":"ad1b8ad0f4d959631","session_id":"f3804fb2-6446-43d6-8c27-86f0daf65430","uuid":"11f8219f-bb4d-4448-bfd6-561778992705","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:18:38.419Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b43d006ee8ccb3e4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
